Tue Sep 22 2026 (UTC) — WP2 pre-freeze work item 1: harness recall-eligibility fix + re-baseline.

Why this change exists
-----------------------
The WP2 root-cause correction block (evidence register §3) recorded that the harness's recall
channel was INERT: every corpus fixture is a memory-3 record, a v3 record projects trust
`'candidate'` unless a legacy alias binds it, and `isRecallEligible` requires
`trust ∈ {local, team}`. `activate` mutates LIFECYCLE only and can never confer trust.
So the harness measured TWO channels (lexical + semantic) while `docs/bench/graph-gates.md`
described THREE ("recall hits fused by reciprocal rank, k = 60") — an overstatement, and a
vacuous gate: the S2 eligibility fuse at the recall channel had nothing to reject.

The fix is in the HARNESS, not the corpus. The frozen corpora (GRAPH_CORPUS_VERSION = 1,
GRAPH_HELDOUT_CORPUS_VERSION = 2) are untouched. At seed time the harness now stamps each
fixture with a synthetic legacy alias carrying local/valid/current/active verdicts, which is
exactly the mechanism by which a real memory-3 record inherits trust from a migrated v1 record
(`conservativeVerdicts`, packages/memory/src/aliases.ts). Aliases are written through the real
`AliasIndex.upsertAliases` into the fixture's own store (local store for repo-placed records,
global store for global ones), so the fuse sees them through the ordinary recall path.

GRAPH_EVAL_HARNESS_VERSION 2 → 3. This is a MEASUREMENT-FIDELITY bump: it changes what the
harness measures, not what the product does. No retrieval constant, scorer, seed limit, hop
count, budget, threshold or corpus was changed.

Result — the recall channel is live and NON-DISCRIMINATING on these corpora
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Both corpora re-run once with harness v3, on the current tree, into new report files. Every
gate value is IDENTICAL to the harness-v2 reports:

